🟢 LEVEL 1 — NMAP FUNDAMENTALS
1️⃣ Nmap kya hai
Nmap = Network Mapper
"Network mein kaunse hosts hain, kaunse ports open hain aur un ports par kaunsi services chal rahi hain?"

Host alive hai?
        ↓
Kaunse ports open hain?
        ↓
Kaunsi services chal rahi hain?
        ↓
Service ka version kya hai?
        ↓
OS kya ho sakta hai?


🛡️ SOC mein Nmap kyun important hai?
SOC Analyst ko network mein pata hona chahiye:

Kaunse systems exist karte hain
Kaunse ports exposed hain
Kaunsi services running hain
Koi unauthorized service toh nahi
Network baseline mein kya change hua

2️⃣ Nmap Install & Verify
*Kali Linux mein check karo:
</>Bash
nmap --version

*Agar installed nahi hai:
</>Bash
sudo apt update
sudo apt install nmap

3️⃣ First Nmap Scan
Apne authorized lab machine ka IP maan le:
192.168.1.20
</>Bash
nmap 192.168.1.20
Nmap basic scan karega.

Typical output:
PORT     STATE SERVICE
22/tcp   open  ssh
80/tcp   open  http
443/tcp  open  https


4️⃣ Specific Port Scan
*Agar sirf port 22 check karna hai:            *Multiple ports:                          *Range:
nmap -p 22 192.168.1.20                         nmap -p 22,80,443 192.168.1.20            nmap -p 20-100 192.168.1.20

*SOC use
Agar investigation mein specifically SSH aur HTTP check karna hai:
nmap -p 22,80 192.168.1.20

5️⃣ All 65535 TCP Ports
Nmap default scan all 65,535 TCP ports nahi karta.

All TCP ports scan karne ke liye:
nmap -p- 192.168.1.20


DIFFERENECE scan ports SINGLE , RANGE , ALL
           -p 80
            ↓
        Only port 80
          -p 20-100
            ↓
        Ports 20 → 100
            -p-
            ↓
        All TCP ports

6️⃣ Verbose Mode  [-v ---> More information & -vv ----> Even More]
*More information:              *Even more:
nmap -v 192.168.1.20             nmap -vv 192.168.1.20

7️⃣ -n — DNS Resolution Disable
DNS resolution disable:
nmap -n 192.168.1.20

Why?
-n
 ↓
No DNS resolution
 ↓
Potentially faster / less DNS traffic

8️⃣ -Pn — Host Discovery Skip
Important: -Pn ka matlab target actually alive hai, ye guarantee nahi karta. It simply skips the usual host-discovery step.

-Pn bolta hai:
"Host discovery mat karo; assume karo host up hai."
nmap -Pn 192.168.1.20

Kab useful?
Suppose:
    Target
      ↓
    Firewall
      ↓
  Ping blocked
Nmap ko host down lag sakta hai.

9️⃣ Multiple Targets

Do machines:
nmap 192.168.1.20 192.168.1.30
Ya:
nmap 192.168.1.20,30

🔟 Network Range

Suppose lab network:
192.168.1.0/24

Scan:
nmap 192.168.1.0/24
Ye network ke hosts ko scan karega.
Lekin SOC learning ke liye pehle -sn se host discovery samajhna better hai, kyunki full port scanning unnecessarily noisy/heavy ho sakti hai

⭐ Sabse Important Concept
Nmap ko sirf commands ki list mat samajhna.
Har scan ko is chain mein soch:
TARGET
   ↓
HOST DISCOVERY
   ↓
PORT DISCOVERY
   ↓
SERVICE DETECTION
   ↓
VERSION DETECTION
   ↓
OS DETECTION
   ↓
NSE
   ↓
REPORT
   ↓
SOC ANALYSIS

🔥Example:
nmap -sV 192.168.1.20

Conceptually:
192.168.1.20
      ↓
Which ports?
      ↓
Which services?
      ↓
Which versions?
      ↓
Is anything unexpected?



🧪 Aaj ki Practice
Apni Kali + intentionally vulnerable VM/lab par ye commands samajh:

nmap <LAB-IP>
nmap -v <LAB-IP>
nmap -n <LAB-IP>
nmap -Pn <LAB-IP>
nmap -p 22 <LAB-IP>
nmap -p 22,80,443 <LAB-IP>
nmap -p 20-100 <LAB-IP>
nmap -p- <LAB-IP>



